CPython-derived test ports
==========================

The `.spy` test files in this directory (`src/Sharpy.Stdlib.Tests/Spy/cpython/`)
are ports of test methods from the CPython 3.12 standard-library test suite
(`Lib/test/test_*.py`). Each file carries a per-file provenance header naming the
CPython source module and the originating test class/method(s).

The original CPython test code is Copyright (c) 2001-2024 Python Software
Foundation; All Rights Reserved, and is distributed under the terms of the
PYTHON SOFTWARE FOUNDATION LICENSE VERSION 2 (PSF-2.0). See:

    https://docs.python.org/3/license.html

These ports are derivative works of that PSF-2.0 material. They translate
value-level assertions into Sharpy `.spy` `@test` functions; bodies are adapted
(loops unrolled, statically typed, Sharpy-API-shaped) rather than copied verbatim.
Methods that cannot survive Sharpy's static typing / API surface are omitted or
adapted, with the divergence noted at the port site.

Oracle source pin: CPython 3.12.x (see build_tools/cpython_oracle/oracle_sources.py).
Tracking issue: https://github.com/antonsynd/sharpy/issues/1030
